app ecdsa-spec [
  version: "1.0.0",
  description: "Design contract for verifying an ECDSA P-256 / SHA-256 signature (FIPS 186-4 section 6.4.2, SEC 2 secp256r1, what JWS ES256 needs). ECDSA_VERIFY { x, y, message, signature } takes the public key coordinates as 32-byte big-endian padded base64 each, the message as text (hashed as its UTF-8 bytes) and the signature as 64 raw bytes r||s (the JWS form, RFC 7518 section 3.4). It answers ECDSA_VERIFIED { valid } or ECDSA_REFUSED { reason }, reason invalid (not canonical base64), length (x or y not 32 bytes, signature not 64 bytes), range (r or s outside 1..n-1), point (x or y not below p, or the point off the curve y^2 = x^3 - 3x + b; the point at infinity has no coordinates so it is refused here) or bigint (std-bigint refused). valid is true iff X = u1*G + u2*Q is not infinity and X.x mod n equals r, with e = SHA-256(message) as a big-endian integer, w = s^-1 mod n, u1 = e*w mod n, u2 = r*w mod n. Signing is out of scope. Golden vectors (openssl prime256v1 with SHA-256, DER converted to raw r||s; the 15-vector regression gate, each run through orb execute --steps in about 10 s for a verdict and 1 s for a refusal, 1.2 MB peak): key 1 is x=lIDYhkqscUItd6oN2IL11yMr74OBpa10Jmuw1wbtzVE= y=1WSlIjIpQ79tukDvI5mpfuEnky4e3zHM2jcMPAfjGHc=, key 2 is x=lY/t6OaXsTZDtoisaniuJ1PbXnKm8vZkiS3FCMCimKE= y=RIHEgzefs79lptLsuf/LhYrY82LyAFY829Y5yXgpuOk=, the base message is eyJhbGciOiJFUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyIn0 and its key 1 signature is r08lHrsUUqXcowTBwMOzj3Og31xq0X7Rx99FsvH14xGGhlx1QmYcN7w0v7zPephdqbjWkz9ht9c8b11ZeOekgg==. With key 1: the base signature verifies true; message plus an x verifies false (tampered-message); signature byte 40 xor 1 verifies false (tampered-signature); the base signature under key 2 verifies false (wrong-key); r replaced by 32 zero bytes refuses range; s replaced by n refuses range; y with its last byte xor 1 refuses point (off-curve); the first 63 signature bytes refuse length. Literal vectors (VERIFIED true unless stated): x-ge-p: x=/////wAAAAEAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAD///////////////8= y=ZkhceA4vg9ckM71dhKBrtlQcKvMdrocXKL+FahdPk/Q= message=eyJhbGciOiJFUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyIn0 signature=r08lHrsUUqXcowTBwMOzj3Og31xq0X7Rx99FsvH14xGGhlx1QmYcN7w0v7zPephdqbjWkz9ht9c8b11ZeOekgg== -> REFUSED point | y-ge-p: x=lIDYhkqscUItd6oN2IL11yMr74OBpa10Jmuw1wbtzVE= y=/////wAAAAEAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ= message=eyJhbGciOiJFUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyIn0 signature=r08lHrsUUqXcowTBwMOzj3Og31xq0X7Rx99FsvH14xGGhlx1QmYcN7w0v7zPephdqbjWkz9ht9c8b11ZeOekgg== -> REFUSED point | rn-alternative: x=oIag22PTamBzP5WmmWeyCgIKcvju2vQDbW8Y5k/48wU= y=639+I5b/Wxp28k/zV1mK2vBs1xgwCmrt6xhlUyp1Hsc= message=rn-alt signature=AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADWGqk1vA2daFgCjWgmZUNiQwZLP06yUrw8h3bZsrUomjRFuzhc499k9nBckEeILkA== -> VERIFIED true | q-equals-g: x=axfR8uEsQkf4vOblY6RA8ncDfYEt6zOg9KE5RdiYwpY= y=T+NC4v4af5uO5+tKfA+eFivOM1drMV7Oy7ZAaDe/UfU= message=exc1-2 signature=tT5axBvLqL1cYpqYdV2yntyEnSmHNP3Ooi6qGj3fTkl80y9Z04flg9ixhZQAOJoYQmcCU6sFCYT7p4XgLAcBXg== -> VERIFIED true | q-negates-g: x=axfR8uEsQkf4vOblY6RA8ncDfYEt6zOg9KE5RdiYwpY= y=sBy9HAHlgGVxGBS1g/Bh6dQxzKmUzqExNEm/l8hArgo= message=exc2-9 signature=Njh3OhOqjvw+OSNK/oc4g5AalDWZ3lRPo+JkUM4sLr8B5Jg2LFoL60CuYXf4ImwrbNawImVVdRDbJgY3H8+4yQ== -> VERIFIED true | forged-q-equals-g: x=axfR8uEsQkf4vOblY6RA8ncDfYEt6zOg9KE5RdiYwpY= y=T+NC4v4af5uO5+tKfA+eFivOM1drMV7Oy7ZAaDe/UfU= message=forge100497933 signature=uy1CDw+ICAsQo9ayqgXhGrJxWUV5XoIpRRq9gfHWntdyFYNw0mmppa5ljzP+O4kLk/RIs6WqPIFPQm3Ls5T7Nw== -> VERIFIED false | forged-q-negates-g: x=axfR8uEsQkf4vOblY6RA8ncDfYEt6zOg9KE5RdiYwpY= y=sBy9HAHlgGVxGBS1g/Bh6dQxzKmUzqExNEm/l8hArgo= message=forge305582123 signature=djGpkvDOWDUFxq8HWNVWPass0x7jFRKIYsM6T7d061PEqurBN9x2+w8XowB+YqoKHfn9eJxlOTgrBTfmWv+yKg== -> VERIFIED false. x-ge-p is the smallest on-curve x offset by p, so silent reduction would accept it. rn-alternative has R.x in [n, p), so only the r + n comparison verifies it. q-equals-g and q-negates-g are valid signatures under key Q = G and Q = -G whose u1 and u2 both have bit 255 set, so the first add hits the double (sum equals the point) and infinity (sum negates it) branches. The two forged vectors exist because an add that collapsed to (0,0,0) once accepted any signature of this shape: random r and s under Q = G and Q = -G, both u1 and u2 of 256 bits, must verify false."
]

orbital EcdsaSpec {
  expects entity EcdsaRun [runtime] {
    id : string!
  }
  expects trait EcdsaVerifier {
    state idle {
      ECDSA_VERIFY -> idle
    }
    emits {
      ECDSA_VERIFIED { valid : boolean! }
      ECDSA_REFUSED { reason : string! }
    }
  }
  expects page "/ecdsa" -> EcdsaVerifier
}
